&lt;p&gt;The feature matrix lists environments under the Enterprise plan. Layer5 Cloud does not refuse environment actions because of the plan.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Workspace and Environment Reference</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1349/cloud/reference/workspaces-and-environments/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1349/cloud/reference/workspaces-and-environments/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This page states how workspaces and environments behave, exactly. For the model, read the &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1349/cloud/concepts/workspaces/"&gt;Workspaces&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1349/cloud/concepts/environments/"&gt;Environments&lt;/a&gt; concepts. For tasks, use the &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1349/cloud/guides/workspaces/"&gt;workspace guides&lt;/a&gt;. For every endpoint&amp;rsquo;s schema, see the &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1349/cloud/reference/api-reference/rest/"&gt;REST API Reference&lt;/a&gt;, and for base URL and authentication see the &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1349/cloud/reference/api-reference/"&gt;Cloud API&lt;/a&gt;. All paths below sit under &lt;code&gt;/api&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id="fields-defaults-and-limits" class="heading-link"&gt;
 Fields, defaults, and limits
 &lt;a href="#fields-defaults-and-limits" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink to this heading"&gt;🔗&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
 &lt;thead&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;Property&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;Workspace&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;Environment&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/thead&gt;
 &lt;tbody&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Name&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Up to 255 characters. Not required or unique on the API.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Up to 255 characters. Not required or unique on the API.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Description&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Up to 255 characters. May be empty.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Up to 255 characters. May be empty.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Organization&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Required on create. Fixed for the life of the workspace.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Required on create (&lt;code&gt;organizationId is required&lt;/code&gt;). Fixed for the life of the environment.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Owner&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;The user who created it.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Not recorded on create.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Starting state&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;No teams, environments, designs, or views.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;No connections, in no workspace.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Kind&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Single kind.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Ordinary when created through the API. Platform-provisioned environments exist and are protected.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Update&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Only the fields sent change.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Name and description are both replaced; an omitted field becomes empty.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Plan check&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;None.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;None. The feature matrix lists environments under Enterprise.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Count limits&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;None. An organization must keep at least one workspace.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;None.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Layer5 Cloud creates &lt;strong&gt;My Workspace&lt;/strong&gt; in any organization that has no workspace.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>